# local-llm

A local-first LLM server prototype.

## What it does

- `local-llm start` opens a terminal flow
- You paste either:
  - a local model path, or
  - a direct download URL
- It saves the model into a local registry so you do not need to enter it again
- It starts a FastAPI server and opens the model settings page in your browser
- It exposes:
  - `POST /chat`
  - `POST /v1/chat/completions`
  - `GET /models`
  - `POST /models/load`
  - `POST /settings`

## Install

```bash
pip install -e .
```

## Start

```bash
local-llm start
```

## Notes

- Models are stored in `~/.local-llm/models/`
- Registry data lives in `~/.local-llm/registry.toml`
- Settings live in `~/.local-llm/config.toml`

This is a prototype designed to be easy to extend.
